@startuml

salt
{
  <b>CHANGE THE CONVENTION A PARTY USES FOR ONE KIND</b>  { Kind: swap | Document | Change | Reach }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>swap</b>, party ACCOUS
      --
      Owner: <b>party</b> | Term columns: 7 | Documents: <b>320</b> | Distinct term sets: <b>201</b>
      Filter: "^AED-EIBOR-3M-SWAP     "  <i>takes id_one_of only: it filters by key, not by a term</i>
      --
      {#
        Document | Terms in words | Version
        AED-SWAP | AED - ModifiedFollowing - 30/360 - 2d | v1
        <b>AED-EIBOR-3M-SWAP</b> | the same terms as AED-SWAP | v1
        EUR-6M-SWAP | TARGET - ModifiedFollowing - ACT/360 | v3
        ... 317 more documents ...
      }
    } | {
      <b>AED-EIBOR-3M-SWAP</b>  (key, not a name: 201 names cover 320 documents)
      --
      {#
        Term | Value | Source
        Fixed Calendar | ^AED^ | from calendar_names
        Fixed Frequency | ^Annual^ | from payment_frequencies
        Fixed Convention | ^ModifiedFollowing^ | from business_day_convention_types
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | ^ACT/360^ | from day_count_fraction_types
        Index | ^AED-EIBOR-3M^ | from floating_index_types
        Float Frequency | ^Semi-Annual^ | from payment_frequencies
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | ^Compounding^ | from sub_periods_coupon_types
      }
      --
      <b>Which act is this?</b>
      (o) Use a different document    <i>pick an existing row</i>
      ( ) Correct this document       <i>write a new version of this row</i>
      <i>A third act, terms no document states, is a different journey.</i>
      [ Review the change ]
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>Review, and what the change reaches</b>
      --
      2 fields differ from version 1. Nothing is written until you confirm.
      {#
        Field | v1 | staged
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | 30/360 | ACT/360
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty) | Compounding
      }
      --
      <b>It reaches every definition of this party.</b>
      The run's conventionsFile is built from the party's whole conventions
      document and the bound configuration is not read, so this change reaches
      <b>all 22</b> of ACCOUS's definitions.
      <i>On a tenant kind it reaches every party of the tenant.</i>
      --
      <b>The reach looks narrower than it is.</b>
      ACCOUS binds one configuration, US conventions, for all 22 of its definitions,
      so the party's reach and the configuration's reach coincide and nobody sees
      the difference. A party binding two conventions configurations would still
      be reached in both, and the screen would have said one.
      --
      <b>It does not reach a run already produced.</b>
      A run keeps the file it ran with; its outputs and its errors are that run's.
      --
      <b>Nothing records which run read which version.</b>
      A comparison across this change compares two different sets of terms.
      --
      Change reason: [ ^system.reference_data_correction v ]  Commentary: "^ACT/360 per the 2026 term sheet        "
      [ Cancel ] | [ Save ]
    } | {
      <b>Outcome</b>
      --
      <b>AED-EIBOR-3M-SWAP is saved as version 2</b>
      by m.okafor at 2026-10-18 09:41, reason system.reference_data_correction
      --
      <b>What the write did not do</b>
      It did not mark this document as the one a run takes: no such mark exists.
      It did not retire version 1: a convention is retired by a delete.
      --
      <b>History</b>  version: { <b>v1</b> | v2 }
      {#
        Field | v1
        Fixed Day Count Fraction | 30/360
        Sub-Periods Coupon Type | (empty)
      }
      [ Back to the kind ]
      --
      <b>Refused</b>  (its own screen, no rail place)
      The write was refused. The document keeps version 1.
      {#
        Refusal | Detail
        Raised on | Review, and what the change reaches
        kind | must_match_version: the row moved since you read it
      }
      <i>result.success = false carries no field-level record.</i>
    }
  }
}

@enduml
